      "General contracting on a rural single-family home, which describes about 95 percent of the housing here, often mixes exterior and interior work: an entry or mudroom rework, new windows, a basement finished at the same time as a kitchen. We coordinate the sequence and act as your contact. Structural changes need a licensed professional and the appropriate permit, inspections go through the town's building department, and plumbing and electrical go to licensed trades."
