      "Some 61 percent of the housing was built before 1980, and anything painted before 1978 could contain lead. We are an EPA Lead-Safe (RRP) certified firm and test before sanding old trim, doors and window sashes. Homes of the late 1960s and 1970s often have stained wood trim, paneling in dens and basements, and textured ceilings, all of which need their own prep before paint. Ashby is about 24 miles from Hudson, so we set a clear start date and plan full working days on site."
