      "answer": "They can be painted, but knots often bleed through ordinary primer as yellow or brown spots. We clean the surface, scuff-sand the finish, and use a shellac-based or stain-blocking primer over the knots before the full primer coat. Grooves between boards get extra attention so paint doesn't pool. Once sealed properly, the wall takes latex paint like any other surface."
