      "Most decks are pressure-treated pine, with some cedar and some composite. Treated pine usually needs fresh stain on horizontal surfaces every few years, depending on sun and foot traffic, while railings last longer. Composite doesn't take stain but does benefit from cleaning. On older decks we also check ledger flashing and fasteners, since failures there show up as rot near the house wall. Ashby is about 24 miles from Hudson, so wash day and stain day are planned together."
