      "Water damage is the other big category. Ice dams at roof edges, a leaking tub surround or a burst pipe in an unheated space can soften drywall and stain ceilings. We cut out damaged sections back to solid framing, install new board, tape, finish and prime, then paint. Texture on walls and ceilings is matched by hand as closely as the existing surface allows. For homes built before 1978, we follow lead-safe practices whenever sanding or cutting disturbs old paint."
