      "answer": "Yes. The upper porch can be done as its own job, but we plan for drips reaching the porch below, so the lower unit's surface gets covered while we work. The household downstairs should know the schedule, because they may need to keep windows closed and stay out of the area on cleaning and staining days. Once the stain has dried, the upper porch goes back to normal use and the lower one is uncovered and cleaned."
