      "With 97 percent of homes owner-occupied, most projects are families improving the place they live. We coordinate carpentry, drywall, paint and licensed plumbers and electricians. We hold no Construction Supervisor License, so load-bearing changes go to a licensed professional with the proper permit, and inspections are handled through the town's building department. One National Register listing, the Benjamin Caryl House, points to how old some of the town's housing is, and older homes deserve extra care around original materials."
