      "We handle drywall, trim, cabinet installation and finishes, and we coordinate licensed plumbers and electricians. Structural work, such as removing a bearing wall or cutting new openings in exterior walls, requires a licensed professional and the appropriate permit, and we do not perform it in-house. Permits and inspections go through the town's building department when the scope requires them. Some houses of this period have aluminum branch wiring or basement moisture, both worth addressing before new finishes go in."
