      "answer": "We are. As the general contractor, we set the order of work and confirm each trade's date before the previous one finishes. If a plumbing inspection is delayed, we move drywall to match rather than leaving you to sort it out. You still choose finishes and approve changes, but you shouldn't have to referee the schedule. Inspections go through the town's building department wherever the work requires them."
