      "answer": "Often at least part of it does. Kitchens of that era were wired for a few lights and a refrigerator, not modern counters full of appliances, and older wiring types can be unsafe to extend. A licensed electrician evaluates what is there and what the new layout needs. We coordinate that work so it happens while walls are open, before insulation, drywall and paint close everything up."
