      "Harsh winters and heavy snow also cause interior damage. Ice dams along the roof edge push water back into ceilings and upper walls, and older Victorians and Colonials with plaster on wood lath can sag or crack once they get wet. Mid-century Ranches and Capes near the 1966 median year may have rock lath or early drywall. We cut out wet or damaged material, reattach loose plaster where it can be saved, and match the surrounding texture. We paint to a corner or break so the patch blends better."
