      "answer": "It can be, with the right precautions. If the paint predates 1978, we treat it as lead-containing unless tests show otherwise. We seal the room with plastic, keep dust down with misting, use HEPA vacuums and clean thoroughly before anyone goes back in. Children and pregnant family members should stay out of the work area until cleanup is done. The other unit may need notice if a shared wall is involved."
