      "answer": "Yes, and for an absentee owner it is often the practical route. Managing trades yourself means coordinating arrival dates, inspections and who fixes what when one trade damages another's work. In an older multi-family building with tenants, shared utilities and limited parking, those handoffs are where projects stall. We act as the single contact, schedule licensed plumbers and electricians, handle the carpentry, drywall and finish work ourselves, and keep you informed at each step."
