      "answer": "Often, if the old paint is well bonded. We test adhesion with tape after scoring a small area. Where it holds, we scuff-sand, clean and prime with a bonding primer. Where it lifts, the loose paint has to come off, and on cabinets from before 1978 that sanding follows lead-safe practices. Previously painted rental cabinets often have drips and brush marks, so extra sanding time usually goes into leveling the old coat."
