      "answer": "Mostly coordination. Shared basements, meters and shut-offs mean a plumber or electrician working on one unit may need brief access to shared spaces or a short utility interruption, and we schedule those with notice. Dust control matters more with shared stairs and halls. Sound carries through floors in these buildings, so loud demolition stays within reasonable hours. The scope itself is much like a single-family remodel."
