    "faq": {
      "question": "Who do I call if the electrician and the plumber disagree about where something goes?",
      "answer": "You call us. Sorting out conflicts between trades is the main reason to hire a general contractor. When two trades need the same wall cavity or the same stretch of basement ceiling, we look at the plan, talk with both licensed trades, and settle the order and routing before work continues. If the change affects the layout or finishes you chose, we explain the options and let you decide."
    },
