      "answer": "No. Aluminum siding can be painted if it is cleaned well and the chalky oxidized surface is removed. A bonding primer may be needed where the factory finish has worn through. Removing the siding usually uncovers wood clapboard with old lead paint that needs repair, prep and a separate plan. Some owners choose that route for appearance, but it is a much bigger job. We can talk through both options at the estimate."
