      "answer": "Usually yes. We remove the doors and drawer fronts and finish them away from the unit, so the kitchen is without doors for several days but still has working counters, sink and appliances. The boxes are cleaned, primed and painted in place, with masking and ventilation. Tenants need to empty the cabinets beforehand and keep the area clear on work days. If there are older built-ins with lead paint, those follow lead-safe practices."
