      "answer": "Yes, once the leak is fixed and the ceiling is dry. We check whether plaster is still attached to the lath, remove loose or damaged sections, and patch with plaster or drywall. The repaired area is primed and painted, and a full ceiling repaint often looks better than a spot. If the building predates 1978, the work follows lead-safe practices. The residents of that room should keep it clear during the repair."
