      "question": "How do you schedule different trades so they are not waiting on each other?",
      "answer": "We build the schedule backward from the finish. Each trade gets a phase with a clear end point, such as rough wiring complete and inspected before drywall goes up. We confirm dates with each trade the week before and adjust if one phase runs long. Materials are ordered ahead so no one arrives to an empty site. When something unexpected turns up, we tell you right away and update the plan so the next trade is not left waiting."
