      "Winchester has about 3,790 people per square mile and 78 percent single-family homes, a combination that usually means a private backyard, though rarely a large one. Decks on lots like that tend to be modest, often attached to a kitchen or family room added onto an older house, and they sit close to the next yard. Staining there has to account for overspray, cleaning runoff flowing toward a neighbor's garden, and the noise of a pressure washer early in the day.",
      "Older houses often gained decks decades after they were built, so the framing and boards may come from different periods. Pressure-treated pine is common; some owners chose cedar or tropical hardwood, which need oil-based or hardwood-specific finishes. Close lots also bring shade from nearby houses and trees, so boards dry slowly after rain. We check moisture, clean with a product suited to the wood, and choose a stain that fits how much sun the deck gets."
