      "Kitchens of the pre-war and post-war decades were generally small and closed, with little counter space and walls that may be load-bearing. Taking those walls out needs a licensed professional's design and the appropriate permit; A&M doesn't do structural work in-house. Licensed plumbers and electricians handle their trades, which we coordinate, and permits and inspections go through the town's building department when required. Pre-1978 surfaces get lead-safe practices during demolition."
