      "answer": "It gets documented and discussed before anything continues in that area. The licensed electrician explains what's there and what code requires to be updated, and we adjust the scope and schedule with you. Knob-and-tube or cloth-insulated wiring is not unusual in homes built before the 1950s. Replacing it while walls are already open is typically far less disruptive than coming back later, but the decision stays yours."
