      "That containment matters more because the median building dates to 1938. Pre-war New England houses were generally clad in wood clapboard or shingles with layered trim, and many have decades of paint on them, some of it likely lead-based. As an EPA Lead-Safe (RRP) certified firm, we test and contain before scraping. Winthrop has five National Register listings, including the Deane Winthrop House and the Highland School, which shows how far back its building history goes. If your house is in a local historic district, check with the town before changing exterior colors."
