      "question": "The cracks in our upstairs ceiling open up every winter. Is our house settling?",
      "answer": "Probably not in a worrying way. In many houses built with roof trusses, the bottom chords rise slightly in winter as the attic gets cold and dry, pulling the ceiling away from interior walls. Retaping won't stop it. Common fixes are to fasten the ceiling edge to blocking instead of the trusses, or to cover the joint with crown molding attached only to the ceiling. If cracks run diagonally from doors or windows instead, have it looked at."
